            <div xml:id="d636">

                <pb facs="1031" n="895" sameAs="frus:frus1888p1/pg895"/>

                <head>No. 636.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Thompson to Mr. Bayard.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Port au Prince Hayti</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1888-06-19"><hi rendition="#italic">June</hi> 19, 1888</date>.
                        (Received June 26.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 189.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have to inform you of the arrival of the
                    French man-of-war <hi rendition="#italic">Du Couëdic</hi> on the 9th and her
                    departure on the 13th instant. The French ship of war <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Bison</hi> is expected.</p>
                <p>H. M. S. <hi rendition="#italic">Ready</hi> arrived here the 13th, relieving the
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Wrangler</hi>, the latter returning to Jamaica.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">John E. W.
                    Thompson.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
